<title>PORTUGAL: Sonae, EDP to seek phone licence.</title>
<headline>Sonae, EDP to seek phone licence.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-controlled utility group EDP Electricidade de Portugal, Sonae, Maxitel, Transgas and Gas de Portugal will bid jointly for a third Portuguese cellular phone licence, EDP said in a statement.  </p>
<p>EDP said that other partners, including international companies, could still join the group before bidding starts in September.</p>
<p>It said that retailing group and real estate group Sonae would hold a controlling stake in the consortium, with EDP and its gas company allies taking the second biggest share.</p>
<p>Transgas and Gas de Portugal are state-owned companies. Maxitel is a privately-owned telecommunications company.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
